1.m:
Now, those [sāmans] that are named after the verse are named from the mother's side;

now, those that are named after the sāman are named from the father's side;

now, those that are named after the tone are named from Prajāpati.

2.m:
The Gāyatrīs are white in appearance; variegated is the appearance of the Uṣṇihs;

tawny is the appearance of the Kakubhs; black after that is [the metre] belonging to the Anuṣṭubh;

red is the Bṛhatī, but dark blue again is the Paṅkti;

golden is the appearance of the Triṣṭubhs; pale white is said to be that of the Jagatī.

And furthermore, as for whatever other metres there are, brown is theirs after that;

mongoose-coloured, however, is that of the single-line [metres]; of two-line [metres], reddish-brown is declared.

Variegated, white, and black in appearance, connected with the Ṛgveda, Yajurveda, Sāmaveda, and the Brāhmaṇas:
